message:
Update a map for non existent key will raise a KeyError, not ArgumentError

```
iex(7)> map = %{:a => 1, 2 => :b}
%{2 => :b, :a => 1}
iex(8)> %{map | :c => 3}
** (KeyError) key :c not found in: %{2 => :b, :a => 1}
```

Documentation for options on gen.{context, html, json} (#2165)

* Typo fix in phx.gen.schema documentation

* Documenting the options on phx.gen.{context, html, json}

Correctly deduplicate multiclauses

In the previous version, module part analysis would treat multiclauses as distinct functions. That cause problems with the `StrictModuleLayout`.

For example:

```
@impl
def handle_call(...), do:
def handle_call(...), do:
```

The second clause would be incorrectly interpreted as a public function.

Rename Application.format_reason/1 to format_error

Makes the function name consistent with OTP modules, which all use
format_error to format reason in {:error, reason}

Fix identention inside lists

The following commands were used to find the buggy strings:
`ag "[
]\ {4}\[*-]([^
]+[
])+\ {7,}"`
`ag "[
]\ {4}[-*]([^
]+[
])(\ {4,}[^
]+[
])+\ {7,}"`

Fix port message format (#5658)

In the documentation it states that the port data format is

    {port, {:port, data}}

but the examples show it is

    {port, {:data, data}}

Fixed this in the documentation.

add typespecs for errors (#256)

* add typespecs for errors

* change error type to {:error, any}

Only error for duplicate map keys in matches (#9748)

In matches we will error:

    %{a: :b, a: :c} = %{a: :b}

In normal expressions we will only warn:

    %{a: :b, a: :c}

test before_encode_and_sign & after_encode_and_sign hooks (#234)

* verify before_encode_and_sign and after_encode_and_sign hooks are called; allow after_encode_and_sign to return {:error, error}

* credo suggestions

Fix refactoring UnusedOperation

@funs_with_return_values has to be `nil` to mean "all of the functions".

Refs #594

Do not unquote AST twice

Instead of generating

    def __absinthe_type__(:foo_bar), do: unquote(ast)
    def __absinthe_type__("FooBar"), do: unquote(ast)

We generate:

    def __absinthe_type__(:foo_bar), do: unquote(ast)
    def __absinthe_type__("FooBar"), do: __absinthe_type__(:foo_bar)

This considerably reduces the size of the generated code.
Compilation times went from 1.8s to 1.2s in a sample schema.

Compress registry tables by default (#1058)

@benwilson512 sent a PR to Elixir to support compressed
tables. This enables it by default on the Registry.
